h4. Posts

A post is one image or video plus its tags, rating, source and relationships. Search by typing tags into the search box; a post matches when it carries every tag you typed. Prefix a tag with "-" to exclude it, and use "~" for "any of these".

h4. What you can see depends on who you are

Three things decide whether a post appears for you, and they are separate rules:

* [b]Your account level.[/b] Below Member, a search shows at most 20 posts per page. See [[help:users]].
* [b]Gated content.[/b] Posts carrying certain tags do not exist for signed-out visitors at all -- not in results, not in counts, not in navigation -- and are listed but withheld for signed-in accounts below Gold. See [[help:censored_tags]].
* [b]Deleted posts[/b] are removed from every search for everyone below Admin.

Your blacklist hides things on top of that. Hidden is not gone: a blacklisted post still loads by direct link. See [[help:blacklists]].

h4. When the page loads but the image does not

The booru holds no image bytes. Every image is served from separate storage through an authorisation service, and your browser is allowed to fetch it only while you hold a valid session. If a page renders and its image does not, it is almost always your session, not the post: sign in again, or sign in to the chat client, which signs you in here with no extra clicks.

h4. Where posts come from

Most posts arrive through the pipeline -- images posted in the community's chat rooms, and images collected from elsewhere -- already tagged by the taggers. You can upload directly too. See [[help:upload]].

h4. On a post page

* [b]Tags[/b], grouped by who put them there. See [[help:autotags]].
* [b]Rating[/b]: g (general), s (sensitive), q (questionable), e (explicit).
* [b]Parent and children[/b], if the post is a variant of another. See [[help:post_relationships]].
* [b]Pools[/b] the post belongs to. See [[help:pools]].
* [b]Source[/b]: where the image came from, when known.

Comments and notes are not part of this site.
